the following gives the length of the curve defined by the parametric equations\n$$\n\\displaystyle x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t),\\,y=6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\n$$\nfrom $t=0$ to $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ (shown above)?" :question/worked-solution "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t))=-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t))=6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{(-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t))^{2}+(6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t))^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{25{sin}^{2}⁡(5t)+36{cos}^{2}⁡(t)}\\,\\text{d}t\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186401034 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "925080f9-1488-5ed3-9988-57bac8e25aa1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{1}t\\sqrt{9{t}^{2}+2t+4}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401036} {:answer/id #uuid "8b14ae74-d72b-5c6f-bfb4-9fdf19b4b592" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}t\\sqrt{9{t}^{2}+4}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401037} {:answer/id #uuid "c911c453-c1b3-506d-a7de-c8341e32d5e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}t\\sqrt{18{t}^{2}+8}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401038} {:answer/id #uuid "69aeb839-370f-503b-8dde-d870cf822808" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{1}t\\sqrt{3{t}^{2}+2}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401039} {:answer/id #uuid "e1915447-2ced-5598-8af5-d918f3a8a810" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}t\\sqrt{18{t}^{2}+24t+8}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401040}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c911c453-c1b3-506d-a7de-c8341e32d5e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}t\\sqrt{18{t}^{2}+8}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401038} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ac60323-fbe0-5435-bfb2-619a71c7a175" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401035}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "dddf8a10-d360-5144-aae4-5bd6e2bd6915" :question/math-academy-id "q-15174" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the length of the curve defined by the parametric equations\n$$\n\\displaystyle x={t}^{3}+{t}^{2},\\,y={t}^{3}-{t}^{2}\n$$\nfrom $t=0$ to $t=1$ ?" :question/worked-solution "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}+{t}^{2})=3{t}^{2}+2t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-{t}^{2})=3{t}^{2}-2t\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{{(3{t}^{2}+2t)}^{2}+{(3{t}^{2}-2t)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{9{t}^{4}+12{t}^{3}+4{t}^{2}+9{t}^{4}-12{t}^{3}+4{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{18{t}^{4}+8{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}t\\sqrt{18{t}^{2}+8}\\,\\text{d}t\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186401041 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b85309c-59d7-5810-84c4-7ea68f827ebf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{3{sin}^{2}⁡t+2{cos}^{2}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401043} {:answer/id #uuid "cdd04e4b-26ba-5e0d-9091-43c5f06e6bd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401044} {:answer/id #uuid "eb350998-6cb3-5e21-b128-0e21ffcf76a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{9{sin}^{2}⁡t+4{cos}^{2}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401045} {:answer/id #uuid "9f297950-b005-5b22-b845-7190b859cf3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{4{sin}^{2}⁡t+9{cos}^{2}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401046} {:answer/id #uuid "a99448ba-c640-5e57-a298-7dcd50a71e96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(9{sin}^{2}⁡t+4{cos}^{2}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401047}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb350998-6cb3-5e21-b128-0e21ffcf76a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{9{sin}^{2}⁡t+4{cos}^{2}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401045} :answer-field/id #uuid "9286f2bc-6874-57c4-a822-f4b4566f80e0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401042}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "9a2f2890-829e-5660-aa0e-71dea52c1f55" :question/math-academy-id "q-15178" :question/problem "![](images/ca/ca290e8fd51edddf4381ec267b8e0a5692d0e52bd2a36b7d43ab89cbeb5cf00d.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the length of the curve defined by the parametric equations\n$$\n\\displaystyle x=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\n$$\nfrom $t=0$ to $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ (shown above)?" :question/worked-solution "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{9{sin}^{2}⁡t+4{cos}^{2}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186401048 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41c46a2e-4e00-5991-99c9-9dc68c9a9598" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡(3t)+{cos}^{2}⁡(t)}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401050} {:answer/id #uuid "2499ce46-f979-5a96-92be-fd0c7ac31bf7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡(3t)+{cos}^{2}⁡(t)}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401051} {:answer/id #uuid "61eb1149-6ab5-5e3a-8377-404854e1b082" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{2{sin}^{2}⁡(3t)+{cos}^{2}⁡(t)}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401052} {:answer/id #uuid "7ed903c6-dd0e-5b89-95d6-7cb6b868a842" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{3{sin}^{2}⁡(t)+{cos}^{2}⁡(3t)}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401053} {:answer/id #uuid "d4b764bb-1a8d-5c44-bf30-3132c5443550" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡(t)+{cos}^{2}⁡(3t)}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401054}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2499ce46-f979-5a96-92be-fd0c7ac31bf7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡(3t)+{cos}^{2}⁡(t)}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401051} :answer-field/id #uuid "d340f787-388c-5296-b3a4-86e39060db0c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401049}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "243b404d-a4f2-57e8-bc56-d916439edf0e" :question/math-academy-id "q-15182" :question/problem "![](images/d6/d683c3960705fa32d11826008a9844c51c8e59e38f5158fce7f4e44c31b97ca9.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the length of the curve defined by the parametric equations\n$$\n\\displaystyle x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t),\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\n$$\nfrom $t=0$ to $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ (shown above)?" :question/worked-solution "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t))=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t))=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t))^{2}+(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t))^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{9{sin}^{2}⁡(3t)+9{cos}^{2}⁡(t)}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡(3t)+{cos}^{2}⁡(t)}\\,\\text{d}t\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186401866 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a58988e-9e60-53e1-9ccc-6195ac2bdc85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}-1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401868} {:answer/id #uuid "c4824b8b-2ed7-5c3c-ae44-9e7e39c2adaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+4}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401869} {:answer/id #uuid "8e755153-eb7c-5c80-ac13-6bd2f55ebc06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{{e}^{t}-1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401870} {:answer/id #uuid "8dadc22b-b156-5944-b045-f3c498f81787" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{{e}^{t}+2}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401871} {:answer/id #uuid "89771be0-5923-5fe1-8923-30d66256f236" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401872}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "89771be0-5923-5fe1-8923-30d66256f236" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401872} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3d97d84-3165-5293-95f8-8ad9ae1b81ff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401867}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a60afb71-a1f2-5589-86e8-84aaf38f221a" :question/math-academy-id "q-21353" :question/problem "![](images/4a/4aa2bca8faab077c47fb968882579233babe7d323ba3120088e8ea5599fbd570.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the length of the curve defined by the parametric equations\n$$\n\\displaystyle x={e}^{t},\\,y=t\n$$\nfrom $t=0$ to $t=2$ (shown above)?" :question/worked-solution "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})={e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{({e}^{t})^{2}+(1)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+1}\\,\\text{d}t\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536251 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "823bacc4-fbf4-5389-a64d-7f110af210f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{\\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} - 8 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 16}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536257} {:answer/id #uuid "b1908ef3-9a59-519b-acc4-937544a98115" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{4 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} - 4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 16}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536260} {:answer/id #uuid "da996d42-8849-55ec-90c9-24d03293b7da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{4 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} - 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 4}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536263} {:answer/id #uuid "e690a093-9d6e-5e96-b42b-b1e6a10c7b97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{5 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} - 8 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 16}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536265} {:answer/id #uuid "f88eedc9-9582-51d0-8e93-1d4dc39010e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-1}^{1}2 \\sqrt{\\frac{5 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}}{2} - 4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 8}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536267}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e690a093-9d6e-5e96-b42b-b1e6a10c7b97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{5 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} - 8 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 16}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536265} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0aa5001-4107-5eed-9d7a-c928d1a5af00" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536261}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "3d087f2d-2ebd-593b-99f4-2f7d8b955fc6" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the length of the curve defined by the parametric equations\n$$\n\\displaystyle x=2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},\\,y=4 t + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\n$$\nfrom $t=-1$ to $t=1$?" :question/worked-solution "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL=\\int_{t_1}^{t_2}\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\right)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)=- 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(4 t + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)=4 - \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}.\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L&=\\int_{t_1}^{t_2}\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\right)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{\\left(- 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)^2+\\left(4 - \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{4\\sin^2(t)+16-8\\sin(t)+\\sin^2(t)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{5 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} - 8 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 16}\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536259 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33f965c4-fbec-5f3e-bd10-d91dfacf69b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{\\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} - 12 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 36}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536250} {:answer/id #uuid "60669a53-3aed-5918-b3f4-8e5a84fd9f6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{6 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} - 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 6}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536253} {:answer/id #uuid "6c64d5d6-5878-535e-b41c-c5a9b90dab81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{5 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} - 12 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 36}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536255} {:answer/id #uuid "88fe9426-0f87-5f70-8eb7-902bdf8d204c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-1}^{1}2 \\sqrt{\\frac{5 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}}{2} - 6 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 18}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536258} {:answer/id #uuid "f0ef1627-d52e-5173-88ab-e3d2d569cba3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{4 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} - 6 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 36}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536266}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6c64d5d6-5878-535e-b41c-c5a9b90dab81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{5 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} - 12 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 36}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536255} :answer-field/id #uuid "6442eb85-5a10-5773-ae71-85fcdc75c579" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536254}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "aaf9a5e6-550e-5e3c-a669-b1b77faa6305" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the length of the curve defined by the parametric equations\n$$\n\\displaystyle x=2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},\\,y=6 t + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\n$$\nfrom $t=-1$ to $t=1$?" :question/worked-solution "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL=\\int_{t_1}^{t_2}\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\right)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)=- 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(6 t + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)=6 - \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}.\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L&=\\int_{t_1}^{t_2}\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\right)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{\\left(- 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)^2+\\left(6 - \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{4\\sin^2(t)+36-12\\sin(t)+\\sin^2(t)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{5 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} - 12 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 36}\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536262 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bbdcba2-43d5-5f97-ba9a-abe6720ab953" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{\\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} - 10 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 25}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536247} {:answer/id #uuid "2a7f0612-5fd7-52ee-a70e-130a3ff03c98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{5 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} - 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 5}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536248} {:answer/id #uuid "584cd63a-6dbd-5230-a7bd-aa0566917524" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{5 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} - 10 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 25}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536252} {:answer/id #uuid "6e4e6377-6f1f-53d3-8531-5768b844347b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{4 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} - 5 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 25}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536256} {:answer/id #uuid "dca55a99-6225-5828-a80f-9bcf4961a649" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-1}^{1}2 \\sqrt{\\frac{5 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}}{2} - 5 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\frac{25}{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536264}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "584cd63a-6dbd-5230-a7bd-aa0566917524" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{5 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} - 10 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 25}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536252} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ab4e613-7957-55a0-906b-50526e244224" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536249}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "caa6b69c-57ee-5447-869e-070cda4c11ac" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the length of the curve defined by the parametric equations\n$$\n\\displaystyle x=2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},\\,y=5 t + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\n$$\nfrom $t=-1$ to $t=1$?" :question/worked-solution "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL=\\int_{t_1}^{t_2}\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\right)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)=- 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(5 t + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)=5 - \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}.\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L&=\\int_{t_1}^{t_2}\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\right)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{\\left(- 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)^2+\\left(5 - \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{4\\sin^2(t)+25-10\\sin(t)+\\sin^2(t)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{5 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} - 10 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 25}\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186628485 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bdb0d74-cabe-51aa-b3f6-04caf48406fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628014} {:answer/id #uuid "dd9396a0-4e0c-5fd4-a24e-e1774ff1e4b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628287} {:answer/id #uuid "f5088243-e09b-5eda-902d-1579f25e0c21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628325} {:answer/id #uuid "f8d4605e-0c29-5436-9640-80f322965784" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628330} {:answer/id #uuid "ff45a88e-f3dd-58d8-a30b-9186609e0833" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628340}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f5088243-e09b-5eda-902d-1579f25e0c21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628325} :answer-field/id #uuid "edd808e5-f01f-54ed-8770-a1cc2d5d53ba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628422}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "b3f89ece-6af6-5b82-ab4c-a0d6b071d3a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-123039" :question/problem "![](images/22/2262a81966190b89ebf03015e85f1c7e749efc2c4d9f8ed822309508d5b75813.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-2t,\\,y=-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,t\\in [0,\\pi ].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-2t)=2(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{{(2(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-1))}^{2}+{(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{4-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+4{cos}^{2}⁡t+4{sin}^{2}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{8-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to the double-angle formula for cosine, $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )=1-2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .$ Substituting $\\theta =\\frac{t}{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{t}{2}) & =1-2{sin}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{t}{2}\\right) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t & =1-2{sin}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{t}{2}\\right) \\\\ 1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & =2{sin}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{t}{2}\\right) \\\\ 8-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & =16{sin}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{t}{2}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{8-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{16{sin}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{t}{2}\\right)}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{t}{2}\\right)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-2\\cdot 4\\cdot {\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{t}{2}\\right)|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =-8(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡0) \\\\  & =-8(0-1) \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722223 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d68d1bd-9b6f-573d-945b-c33996637181" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_0^{\\pi/3}\\sqrt{4\\sin^2(2t)+9\\cos^2(3t)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722210} {:answer/id #uuid "2b059b3a-a88b-57e3-9d7a-0c4a977b7291" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_0^{\\pi/3}\\sqrt{4\\cos^2(2t)+9\\sin^2(3t)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722211} {:answer/id #uuid "9b1c648c-1cdc-58a5-ad74-8de976ea55ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_0^{\\pi/3}\\sqrt{\\cos^2(2t)+\\sin^2(3t)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722221} {:answer/id #uuid "c07e0fb6-6504-53f8-8cd8-52ab25b121ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_0^{\\pi/3}\\sqrt{16\\cos^2(2t)+9\\sin^2(3t)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722224} {:answer/id #uuid "c49ca18a-8c69-59be-b218-43fcb0194e31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_0^{\\pi/3}\\sqrt{2\\cos^2(2t)+3\\sin^2(3t)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722225}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b059b3a-a88b-57e3-9d7a-0c4a977b7291" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_0^{\\pi/3}\\sqrt{4\\cos^2(2t)+9\\sin^2(3t)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722211} :answer-field/id #uuid "176de2e9-220d-5f25-94a2-e32344ffa40b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722209}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c054bd74-1fa8-50dc-aa8f-bc5a2717fef5" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the arc length of the curve defined by\n\n$$\nx=\\sin(2t)-1,\\qquad y=\\cos(3t)+2,\\qquad 0\\le t\\le\\frac{\\pi}{3}.\n$$\n\nThe indicated segment is shown below.\n\n![Parametric curve segment with direction and parameter endpoints](images/39/397d64be37483a28368c36a7bef340c511c9aff9a7e6160e727ba71ea22a18d5.png)\n\nChoose an integral expression. Do not evaluate it." :question/worked-solution "For a parametric curve, use\n\n$$\nL=\\int_a^b\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\right)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating with respect to $t$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}=2\\cos(2t),\\qquad \\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}=-3\\sin(3t).\n$$\n\nSubstitute the derivatives and the parameter limits:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L&=\\int_0^{\\pi/3}\\sqrt{(2\\cos(2t))^2+(-3\\sin(3t))^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\&=\\int_0^{\\pi/3}\\sqrt{4\\cos^2(2t)+9\\sin^2(3t)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe constants $-1$ and $2$ have zero derivatives. The chain rule supplies factors $2$ and $3$, which become $4$ and $9$ when squared. Squaring the negative derivative gives a positive term. The arguments $2t$ and $3t$ differ, so the two squared trigonometric terms cannot be combined using the Pythagorean identity. Keep the parameter limits $0$ and $\\pi/3$ and leave the integral unevaluated."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722226 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a8053d7-97f3-548e-acca-104ed24010e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_0^{1}\\sqrt{1+e^{2t}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722207} {:answer/id #uuid "5c749f94-04a6-509b-ac4c-d009cc36404a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_0^{1}\\sqrt{1+e^t}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722215} {:answer/id #uuid "60957632-0c61-53bf-a0e0-cc272681c62b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_0^{1}\\sqrt{1+2e^{2t}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722216} {:answer/id #uuid "669c3e46-4fb0-5c1a-a350-a948da3d52ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_0^{1}1+e^{2t}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722217} {:answer/id #uuid "8f2bde4b-888e-5c6a-86e1-0dd6ed7db4fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_0^{1}\\sqrt{2+e^{2t}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722220}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0a8053d7-97f3-548e-acca-104ed24010e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_0^{1}\\sqrt{1+e^{2t}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722207} :answer-field/id #uuid "53ac98f8-6b99-55f8-b685-5d3cc6d5c3e2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722214}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "cc3bd690-ca55-553c-a4e9-d792028b4a9b" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the arc length of the curve defined by\n\n$$\nx=t,\\qquad y=e^t,\\qquad 0\\le t\\le 1.\n$$\n\nThe indicated segment is shown below.\n\n![Parametric curve segment with direction and parameter endpoints](images/9d/9d6b750b612ea841f5afb9bc37ed3d774d3051c77a13e2cb691218c051b1d3b6.png)\n\nUse the arc-length formula\n\n$$\nL=\\int_a^b\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\right)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nChoose an integral expression. Do not evaluate it." :question/worked-solution "For a parametric curve, use\n\n$$\nL=\\int_a^b\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\right)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating with respect to $t$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}=1,\\qquad \\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}=e^t.\n$$\n\nSubstitute the derivatives and the parameter limits:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L&=\\int_0^1\\sqrt{1^2+(e^t)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\&=\\int_0^1\\sqrt{1+e^{2t}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquare each derivative and add the squares inside the square root. In particular, $(e^t)^2=e^{2t}$. The integration limits are the given parameter values, $0$ and $1$. This integral is the requested expression; no evaluation is needed."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722227 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d1cf041-607d-518b-806e-b9d4dbf7cf3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_0^{1}e^t\\sqrt{2-\\sin(2t)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722208} {:answer/id #uuid "4a8e1662-d396-5878-a76e-7fc6c090a93e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_0^{1}e^t\\sqrt{2-\\cos(2t)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722212} {:answer/id #uuid "745bd017-bac2-5ce1-ab0a-9d2d622199a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_0^{1}e^t\\sqrt{2+\\sin(2t)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722218} {:answer/id #uuid "8429fb89-5249-5a47-82b1-2b2e2c52e9dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_0^{1}e^{2t}\\sqrt{2-\\sin(2t)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722219} {:answer/id #uuid "a34aa551-dfb3-5350-a473-32a77153dfab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_0^{1}e^t\\sqrt{1-\\sin(2t)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722222}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0d1cf041-607d-518b-806e-b9d4dbf7cf3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_0^{1}e^t\\sqrt{2-\\sin(2t)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722208} :answer-field/id #uuid "4fed248c-2074-5193-a0cb-7175908faeae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722213}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "e0dd8f03-2b52-5c0f-998b-d1530a2830f4" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the arc length of the curve defined by\n\n$$\nx=e^t,\\qquad y=e^t\\cos t,\\qquad 0\\le t\\le 1.\n$$\n\nThe indicated segment is shown below.\n\n![Parametric curve segment with direction and parameter endpoints](images/38/38d4840253365e13b08d93e0cfcf2194e759cb95d7b7fda9ceaec3805dd5556f.png)\n\nChoose an integral expression. Do not evaluate it." :question/worked-solution "For a parametric curve, use\n\n$$\nL=\\int_a^b\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\right)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nApplying the product rule to $y$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}&=e^t,\\\\\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}&=e^t\\cos t-e^t\\sin t=e^t(\\cos t-\\sin t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute the derivatives and the parameter limits:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L&=\\int_0^1\\sqrt{e^{2t}+e^{2t}(\\cos t-\\sin t)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\&=\\int_0^1 e^t\\sqrt{1+\\cos^2t+\\sin^2t-2\\sin t\\cos t}\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\&=\\int_0^1 e^t\\sqrt{2-\\sin(2t)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $y$ requires the product rule. In simplifying the speed, use $\\cos^2t+\\sin^2t=1$ and $2\\sin t\\cos t=\\sin(2t)$. Also, $\\sqrt{e^{2t}}=e^t$ because $e^t>0$. Thus the constant inside the final square root is $2$, and the cross term has a minus sign. Leave the integral unevaluated."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722232 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "134ab2c9-45c4-5f6f-b064-1dcb035735ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_0^3|t-1|\\sqrt{18(t-1)^2+4}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722229} {:answer/id #uuid "6ba89caa-6b38-58b9-96c3-a9a75e97fa37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_0^3|t-1|\\sqrt{18(t-1)^2+24(t-1)+8}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722236} {:answer/id #uuid "d83c9b7c-ecba-5a52-9b73-7bb6b6e9d72d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_0^3|t-1|\\sqrt{18(t-1)^2+8}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722246} {:answer/id #uuid "e0f26ed7-efe9-53a0-8dbb-62f32612c265" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_0^3(t-1)\\sqrt{18(t-1)^2+8}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722247} {:answer/id #uuid "f68ab80c-365a-5aa0-bbf5-8523e42cbbc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_0^3|t-1|\\sqrt{9(t-1)^2+4}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722248}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d83c9b7c-ecba-5a52-9b73-7bb6b6e9d72d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_0^3|t-1|\\sqrt{18(t-1)^2+8}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722246} :answer-field/id #uuid "239d6eda-d3e1-5bab-9d91-db02da163731" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722231}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "3367d970-1fa1-540d-b21b-20689d46bfa4" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the length of the curve defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx&=(t-1)^3+(t-1)^2,\\\\\ny&=(t-1)^3-(t-1)^2.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe parameter runs from $t=0$ to $t=3$.\n\n![](images/c4/c435bdf976da9c9106c81b7620c90acd80f7f6a446703a173a3cc6a18c258757.png)\n\nChoose an integral expression valid on the entire parameter interval. Do not evaluate the integral." :question/worked-solution "For a parametric curve, the arc length is\n\n$$\nL=\\int_a^b\\sqrt{[x'(t)]^2+[y'(t)]^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nDifferentiate both coordinate functions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx'(t)&=3(t-1)^2+2(t-1),\\\\\ny'(t)&=3(t-1)^2-2(t-1).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse $(A+B)^2+(A-B)^2=2A^2+2B^2$ to find the squared speed $v(t)^2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nv(t)^2\n &=18(t-1)^4+8(t-1)^2\\\\\n &=(t-1)^2\\bigl(18(t-1)^2+8\\bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the speed is\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{[x'(t)]^2+[y'(t)]^2}\n=|t-1|\\sqrt{18(t-1)^2+8}.\n$$\n\nHere $t-1$ is negative for $0\\leq t<1$ and positive for $1<t\\leq3$. Neither $t-1$ nor $1-t$ can replace $|t-1|$ on the entire interval. Therefore,\n\n$$\nL=\\int_0^3|t-1|\\sqrt{18(t-1)^2+8}\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nAt $t=1$ both derivatives vanish, so the speed is zero there. The continuous nonnegative speed still gives the arc length across that point."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722234 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01454c7b-a15a-537d-a68d-9f302f25a92a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_0^1\\sqrt{6t+5}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722228} {:answer/id #uuid "89ebdf60-6d10-53f9-9c5f-1e0c354e762a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_0^1\\sqrt{(3t^2+1)^2+(5t-1)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722239} {:answer/id #uuid "92470607-f697-593f-8cf6-606a5fefbebe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_0^1\\sqrt{36t^2+5}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722240} {:answer/id #uuid "9dec0b52-2cc3-53c6-a451-3c03040bd722" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_0^1\\sqrt{36t^2+25}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722241} {:answer/id #uuid "a4a27425-84ed-5636-ab88-a9c3323d5c2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_0^1\\sqrt{1+\\frac{36t^2}{25}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722244}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9dec0b52-2cc3-53c6-a451-3c03040bd722" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_0^1\\sqrt{36t^2+25}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722241} :answer-field/id #uuid "23730e7a-5ef9-524f-9204-46089a1f66a2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722230}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6624d73e-7495-55f3-9764-969c96fa1212" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the length of the curve defined by\n\n$$\nx=3t^2+1,\\qquad y=5t-1,\\qquad 0\\leq t\\leq1?\n$$\n\n![](images/89/89550464608cc7888bc3ec73436c3944252a204954cb0da6c702018910016d65.png)\n\nChoose an integral expression. Do not evaluate the integral." :question/worked-solution "For a parametric curve, the arc length is\n\n$$\nL=\\int_a^b\\sqrt{[x'(t)]^2+[y'(t)]^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nDifferentiate each coordinate with respect to the parameter:\n\n$$\nx'(t)=6t,\\qquad y'(t)=5.\n$$\n\nSubstitute the derivatives and the parameter bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL&=\\int_0^1\\sqrt{(6t)^2+5^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\\n &=\\int_0^1\\sqrt{36t^2+25}\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe constants added to the coordinates disappear on differentiation. Use both coordinate derivatives, rather than the slope $y'(t)/x'(t)$, inside the square root."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722245 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34dd2934-f297-53ac-a97d-8290c37d4255" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-2}^{-1}(-t)\\sqrt{9t^2+4}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722233} {:answer/id #uuid "6ab7e435-970e-58f2-8e44-7a72e5dbe5cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-2}^{-1}(-t)\\sqrt{18t^2+24t+8}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722235} {:answer/id #uuid "7a544ce4-c619-5e2e-9a54-3fefc0265eb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-2}^{-1}t\\sqrt{18t^2+8}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722237} {:answer/id #uuid "7bdbb7f7-ab6a-58b4-9096-a93aa7d6f3ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-2}^{-1}(-t)\\sqrt{18t^2+4}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722238} {:answer/id #uuid "a0edb1f9-9403-5de3-b881-27357039fdd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-2}^{-1}(-t)\\sqrt{18t^2+8}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722243}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a0edb1f9-9403-5de3-b881-27357039fdd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-2}^{-1}(-t)\\sqrt{18t^2+8}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722243} :answer-field/id #uuid "a03e41c5-8ef6-5ce0-b127-b7783d9f425c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722242}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "cf17b8d3-cbfe-586b-b52e-37d4585ad7fd" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the length of the curve defined by\n\n$$\nx=t^3+t^2,\\qquad y=t^3-t^2,\\qquad -2\\leq t\\leq-1?\n$$\n\n![](images/b3/b337ea648faf08f3ce4f904f5327193e34d3d273cf06dc1710f3170241bbc5f5.png)\n\nChoose an integral expression. Do not evaluate the integral." :question/worked-solution "For a parametric curve, the arc length is\n\n$$\nL=\\int_a^b\\sqrt{[x'(t)]^2+[y'(t)]^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nFirst find both derivatives:\n\n$$\nx'(t)=3t^2+2t,\\qquad y'(t)=3t^2-2t.\n$$\n\nThe squared speed $v(t)^2$ is the sum of the squared derivatives. The cross terms cancel:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nv(t)^2\n &=(3t^2+2t)^2+(3t^2-2t)^2\\\\\n &=9t^4+12t^3+4t^2+9t^4-12t^3+4t^2\\\\\n &=18t^4+8t^2=t^2(18t^2+8).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTaking a square root gives $|t|\\sqrt{18t^2+8}$. Since $t<0$ throughout $[-2,-1]$, we have $|t|=-t$. Therefore,\n\n$$\nL=\\int_{-2}^{-1}(-t)\\sqrt{18t^2+8}\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nThe factor $-t$ is positive on this interval. Replacing $|t|$ by $t$ would give a negative integral, which cannot be this arc length."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722476 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07999095-ca96-5d67-bdd1-dfe00594f14c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722475} {:answer/id #uuid "227d0ade-d790-5bec-8aee-9ddf932a6cb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722477} {:answer/id #uuid "5335aebe-4061-5caf-9a3d-c128a1a9f0ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 \\sqrt{6} + 2 \\sqrt{2} + 4 \\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722483} {:answer/id #uuid "cbd008ff-4c83-504c-99dc-bcbdfbd14f8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8 \\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722494} {:answer/id #uuid "da42661a-ef1c-5bd7-abfb-ab5ef8a765af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4 + 2 \\sqrt{2} + 2 \\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722495}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "07999095-ca96-5d67-bdd1-dfe00594f14c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722475} :answer-field/id #uuid "4696181e-e99b-5b5b-a315-f34e2dec382a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722481}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "10785c7c-b806-5380-8f79-962b1040e3fd" :question/problem "Find the exact arc length of the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x&=8 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 10 \\\\ y&=8 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 8 \\\\ t&\\in\\left[\\frac{\\pi}{6},\\frac{5 \\pi}{12}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The arc length is the integral of the nonnegative speed:\n\n$$\nL=\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{5 \\pi}{12}}\\sqrt{(x\\prime(t))^2+(y\\prime(t))^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nDifferentiate both coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\prime(t)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(8 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 10\\right) \\\\ &=8 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} \\\\ y\\prime(t)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(8 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 8\\right) \\\\ &=- 8 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplify the sum of squares:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x\\prime)^2+(y\\prime)^2&=\\left(8 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)^2 \\\\ &\\quad+\\left(- 8 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)^2 \\\\ &=64(\\cos^2 t+\\sin^2 t) \\\\ &=64\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the stated interval, $8\\geq0$, so taking the square root gives\n\n$$\nv(t)=\\sqrt{(x\\prime)^2+(y\\prime)^2}=8.\n$$\n\nIntegrating the speed gives\n\n$$\n\\int 8\\,\\mathrm{d}t=8 t+C.\n$$\n\nEvaluate at both endpoints and subtract:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L&=\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{5 \\pi}{12}}8\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &=\\left[8 t\\right]_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{5 \\pi}{12}} \\\\ &=\\left(\\frac{10 \\pi}{3}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{4 \\pi}{3}\\right) \\\\ &=2 \\pi\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722479 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c42f23d5-a80d-5114-a07d-baad1b8b528e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722493}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c42f23d5-a80d-5114-a07d-baad1b8b528e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722493} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f5edf4c-9c01-5531-9ff8-8c684070ea1f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722486}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "292e768e-8544-5f34-ac65-d92e417ea130" :question/problem "![](images/75/7528bd6a6c7590d73e0d4446b0fcf78183876938fd857565ba9860faaaae2563.png)\n\nFind the exact arc length of the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x&=- \\frac{t^{3}}{3} + t \\\\ y&=t^{2} \\\\ t&\\in\\left[0,3\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$L=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The arc length is the integral of the nonnegative speed:\n\n$$\nL=\\int_{0}^{3}\\sqrt{(x\\prime(t))^2+(y\\prime(t))^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nDifferentiate both coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\prime(t)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(- \\frac{t^{3}}{3} + t\\right) \\\\ &=1 - t^{2} \\\\ y\\prime(t)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(t^{2}\\right) \\\\ &=2 t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplify the sum of squares:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x\\prime)^2+(y\\prime)^2&=\\left(1 - t^{2}\\right)^2 \\\\ &\\quad+\\left(2 t\\right)^2 \\\\ &=t^{4} + 2 t^{2} + 1 \\\\ &=\\left(t^{2} + 1\\right)^2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the stated interval, $t^{2} + 1\\geq0$, so taking the square root gives\n\n$$\nv(t)=\\sqrt{(x\\prime)^2+(y\\prime)^2}=t^{2} + 1.\n$$\n\nIntegrating the speed gives\n\n$$\n\\int t^{2} + 1\\,\\mathrm{d}t=\\frac{t^{3}}{3} + t+C.\n$$\n\nEvaluate at both endpoints and subtract:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L&=\\int_{0}^{3}t^{2} + 1\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &=\\left[\\frac{t^{3}}{3} + t\\right]_{0}^{3} \\\\ &=\\left(12\\right)-\\left(0\\right) \\\\ &=12\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722480 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01a115dd-5975-5da6-9925-96a6ec4f223b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 4 \\sqrt{2} + 6 \\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722474} {:answer/id #uuid "7167d5de-7d72-516b-80e4-595d2c68c1d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 8 \\sqrt{2} + 12 \\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722485} {:answer/id #uuid "89418978-8c93-5f08-9918-1b715fad9eb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 \\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722487} {:answer/id #uuid "8f5daf33-44a0-5ed0-8b61-8f98a00573c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{45 - 16 \\sqrt{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722489} {:answer/id #uuid "9e4834a8-c376-5308-bba2-b79b14d8d3db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{45}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722492}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "01a115dd-5975-5da6-9925-96a6ec4f223b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 4 \\sqrt{2} + 6 \\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722474} :answer-field/id #uuid "5230968d-7f01-5484-a45e-262997965c20" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722482}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "375a2414-43c2-5766-a338-9db435a8994c" :question/problem "![](images/22/22b88fbe643e04cad37a9e7c39f8862a73da413b5f78f8772bc5a3d18f048ed9.png)\n\nFind the exact arc length of the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x&=3 t + 1 \\\\ y&=2 t^{\\frac{3}{2}} \\\\ t&\\in\\left[1,2\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The arc length is the integral of the nonnegative speed:\n\n$$\nL=\\int_{1}^{2}\\sqrt{(x\\prime(t))^2+(y\\prime(t))^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nDifferentiate both coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\prime(t)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(3 t + 1\\right) \\\\ &=3 \\\\ y\\prime(t)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(2 t^{\\frac{3}{2}}\\right) \\\\ &=3 \\sqrt{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplify the sum of squares:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x\\prime)^2+(y\\prime)^2&=\\left(3\\right)^2 \\\\ &\\quad+\\left(3 \\sqrt{t}\\right)^2 \\\\ &=9 t + 9 \\\\ &=\\left(3 \\sqrt{t + 1}\\right)^2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the stated interval, $3 \\sqrt{t + 1}\\geq0$, so taking the square root gives\n\n$$\nv(t)=\\sqrt{(x\\prime)^2+(y\\prime)^2}=3 \\sqrt{t + 1}.\n$$\n\nIntegrating the speed gives\n\n$$\n\\int 3 \\sqrt{t + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}t=2 \\left(t + 1\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}+C.\n$$\n\nEvaluate at both endpoints and subtract:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L&=\\int_{1}^{2}3 \\sqrt{t + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &=\\left[2 \\left(t + 1\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}\\right]_{1}^{2} \\\\ &=\\left(6 \\sqrt{3}\\right)-\\left(4 \\sqrt{2}\\right) \\\\ &=- 4 \\sqrt{2} + 6 \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722484 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23200dbf-f059-5e6e-9c05-c3e3fee466cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722478}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "23200dbf-f059-5e6e-9c05-c3e3fee466cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722478} :answer-field/id #uuid "8cfc3bcb-4dde-5ecd-a872-cc2c264a9cfa" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722488}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "7027c0d8-2a44-5b7d-9fca-b4ca0961b63d" :question/problem "![](images/d5/d53de709940142c4c015fed29446843c18a2995f517d14bb581ef061bb7284d6.png)\n\nFind the exact arc length of the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x&=\\frac{\\left(6 t + 1\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3} \\\\ y&=\\frac{9 t^{2}}{2} \\\\ t&\\in\\left[0,2\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$L=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The arc length is the integral of the nonnegative speed:\n\n$$\nL=\\int_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{(x\\prime(t))^2+(y\\prime(t))^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nDifferentiate both coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\prime(t)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(\\frac{\\left(6 t + 1\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3}\\right) \\\\ &=3 \\sqrt{6 t + 1} \\\\ y\\prime(t)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(\\frac{9 t^{2}}{2}\\right) \\\\ &=9 t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplify the sum of squares:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x\\prime)^2+(y\\prime)^2&=\\left(3 \\sqrt{6 t + 1}\\right)^2 \\\\ &\\quad+\\left(9 t\\right)^2 \\\\ &=81 t^{2} + 54 t + 9 \\\\ &=\\left(9 t + 3\\right)^2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the stated interval, $9 t + 3\\geq0$, so taking the square root gives\n\n$$\nv(t)=\\sqrt{(x\\prime)^2+(y\\prime)^2}=9 t + 3.\n$$\n\nIntegrating the speed gives\n\n$$\n\\int 9 t + 3\\,\\mathrm{d}t=\\frac{9 t^{2}}{2} + 3 t+C.\n$$\n\nEvaluate at both endpoints and subtract:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L&=\\int_{0}^{2}9 t + 3\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &=\\left[\\frac{9 t^{2}}{2} + 3 t\\right]_{0}^{2} \\\\ &=\\left(24\\right)-\\left(0\\right) \\\\ &=24\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722490 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9cd928d8-878f-5a36-bc8d-6335063621b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 \\pi^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722491}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9cd928d8-878f-5a36-bc8d-6335063621b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 \\pi^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722491} :answer-field/id #uuid "f09ec639-cdc7-53ac-b198-fb5135bdc18e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722496}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "97d3157f-92cb-5879-ad52-62faed75af6d" :question/problem "![](images/f9/f9e208d65e95d8e0b64c084e10f2f8f593b819e5f345cdefd292219758602406.png)\n\nFind the exact arc length of the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x&=2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} \\\\ y&=- 2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\\\ t&\\in\\left[0,2 \\pi\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$L=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The arc length is the integral of the nonnegative speed:\n\n$$\nL=\\int_{0}^{2 \\pi}\\sqrt{(x\\prime(t))^2+(y\\prime(t))^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nDifferentiate both coordinates using the product rule; the opposite cross terms cancel:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\prime(t)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) \\\\ &=2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} \\\\ y\\prime(t)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(- 2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) \\\\ &=2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplify the sum of squares:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x\\prime)^2+(y\\prime)^2&=\\left(2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)^2 \\\\ &\\quad+\\left(2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)^2 \\\\ &=4t^2(\\sin^2 t+\\cos^2 t) \\\\ &=4 t^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the stated interval, $2 t\\geq0$, so taking the square root gives\n\n$$\nv(t)=\\sqrt{(x\\prime)^2+(y\\prime)^2}=2 t.\n$$\n\nIntegrating the speed gives\n\n$$\n\\int 2 t\\,\\mathrm{d}t=t^{2}+C.\n$$\n\nEvaluate at both endpoints and subtract:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L&=\\int_{0}^{2 \\pi}2 t\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &=\\left[t^{2}\\right]_{0}^{2 \\pi} \\\\ &=\\left(4 \\pi^{2}\\right)-\\left(0\\right) \\\\ &=4 \\pi^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722499 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28bb6276-1a32-5d6e-9654-d81fb204d605" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\sqrt{\\left(2 - \\pi\\right)^{2} + 4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722500} {:answer/id #uuid "373eed57-b54e-5411-8dbb-a6c1c007c063" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 - 2 \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722501} {:answer/id #uuid "72a958ff-e7c8-5858-b9af-501ba63f94c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32 - 16 \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722502} {:answer/id #uuid "9a675d3b-7858-5fb7-9ab6-c78464f1ae85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8 - 4 \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722503} {:answer/id #uuid "edbd138a-60fc-53f0-b426-86b3bd02f50c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16 - 8 \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722504}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "edbd138a-60fc-53f0-b426-86b3bd02f50c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16 - 8 \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722504} :answer-field/id #uuid "171b9887-6f2c-5f7d-baea-f28f3f1ee0d3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722498}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "1af411eb-a944-5e21-8357-96c6441fc9d1" :question/problem "![](images/37/370c211db91913c03ea76c81376dd33fab749723d1370db80222281e330d03cd.png)\n\nFind the exact arc length of the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x&=4 t - 4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\\\ y&=4 - 4 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} \\\\ t&\\in\\left[0,\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The arc length is the integral of the nonnegative speed:\n\n$$\nL=\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\sqrt{(x\\prime(t))^2+(y\\prime(t))^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nDifferentiate both coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\prime(t)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(4 t - 4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) \\\\ &=4 - 4 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} \\\\ y\\prime(t)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(4 - 4 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) \\\\ &=4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplify the sum of squares:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x\\prime)^2+(y\\prime)^2&=\\left(4 - 4 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)^2 \\\\ &\\quad+\\left(4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)^2 \\\\ &=32\\left(1-\\cos(t)\\right) \\\\ &=64\\sin^2\\left(\\frac{t}{2}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the stated interval, $\\sin\\left(\\frac{t}{2}\\right)\\geq0$, so taking the square root gives\n\n$$\nv(t)=\\sqrt{(x\\prime)^2+(y\\prime)^2}=8 \\sin{\\left(\\frac{t}{2} \\right)}.\n$$\n\nIntegrating, including the constant chain-rule factor, gives\n\n$$\n\\int 8 \\sin{\\left(\\frac{t}{2} \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t=- 16 \\cos{\\left(\\frac{t}{2} \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nEvaluate at both endpoints and subtract:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L&=\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}8 \\sin{\\left(\\frac{t}{2} \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &=\\left[- 16 \\cos{\\left(\\frac{t}{2} \\right)}\\right]_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} \\\\ &=\\left(- 8 \\sqrt{2}\\right)-\\left(-16\\right) \\\\ &=16 - 8 \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722512 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "190749ec-9a21-5cfe-8b76-e8f9bd8bbadc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{9 t^{4} + 16}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722510} {:answer/id #uuid "24c1ce91-8908-52b8-aa36-4e6613f45f5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{t^{4} + 16}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722511} {:answer/id #uuid "8ccfe458-c48b-5cd8-bc0d-4dc54e08bb0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{4 t^{4}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722526} {:answer/id #uuid "a8d0fe08-78dc-58f8-862a-b4e34ecf39c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{81 t^{4} + 16}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722529} {:answer/id #uuid "b5ef01d2-9a36-5791-8d57-69e0a3c39440" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{16 t^{4} + 64}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722531}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "190749ec-9a21-5cfe-8b76-e8f9bd8bbadc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{9 t^{4} + 16}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722510} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2de499e-aabf-5080-971c-a2af2cc45bc6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722539}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "24e8e7ac-592a-52d1-93a3-99241b46eaa9" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the length of the curve defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx&=t^{3} + 3\\\\\ny&=- 4 t + 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfrom $t=0$ to $t=1$?\n\nChoose an integral expression valid on the entire interval. Do not evaluate it.\n\n![](images/6d/6dd336b159235693a0fb6748d1a40635b4a66423880dbc4ac894f466b887f396.png)" :question/worked-solution "For parametric arc length, use\n\n$$\nL=\\int_a^b\\sqrt{[x\\prime(t)]^2+[y\\prime(t)]^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nDifferentiate each coordinate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx'(t)&=3 t^{2}\\\\\ny'(t)&=-4.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquare both derivatives and add:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx'(t)^2+y'(t)^2&=\\bigl(3 t^{2}\\bigr)^2+\\bigl(-4\\bigr)^2\\\\\n&=9 t^{4} + 16.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the given parameter bounds:\n\n$$\nL=\\int_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{9 t^{4} + 16}\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722514 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "009afd31-ecb0-5a3a-b27e-b8e2911824fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-2}^{3}\\sqrt{324 t^{4} + 9}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722505} {:answer/id #uuid "3e717e59-0211-507a-b8ab-d7488e3086e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-2}^{3}\\sqrt{64 t^{4} + 36}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722515} {:answer/id #uuid "4c48bd5a-032b-5628-ad3a-f9410a944f7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-2}^{3}\\sqrt{4 t^{4} + 9}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722516} {:answer/id #uuid "744097cb-7889-52e8-87f2-19354a29adff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/iden