aligned}\nx'(t)&=9 t^{2} + 4 t\\\\\ny'(t)&=9 t^{2} - 4 t.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe cross terms cancel when the two derivative squares are added.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx'(t)^2+y'(t)^2&=162 t^{4} + 32 t^{2}\\\\\n&=(t)^2\\bigl(162 t^{2} + 32\\bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse $\\sqrt{(t)^2}=|t|$. The factor $t$ is nonnegative on this interval. Hence $|t|=t$ here.\n\nUse the given parameter bounds:\n\n$$\nL=\\int_{1}^{3}\\left(t\\right)\\sqrt{162 t^{2} + 32}\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722543 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "029f5f02-9a3a-5420-8cff-30290482d6f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{3}\\left|t - 2\\right|\\sqrt{128 \\left(t - 2\\right)^{2} + 162}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722541} {:answer/id #uuid "1cb1bfc4-9be6-5365-96b3-9a0feea4c151" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{3}\\left|t - 2\\right|\\sqrt{288 \\left(t - 2\\right)^{2} + 288}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722544} {:answer/id #uuid "54faccd6-eecc-514d-bb38-fc31485a5741" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{3}\\left(- t + 2\\right)\\sqrt{288 \\left(t - 2\\right)^{2} + 288}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722549} {:answer/id #uuid "ce610074-5a90-54f0-8399-cb91e4a8db70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{3}\\left|t - 2\\right|\\sqrt{72 \\left(t - 2\\right)^{2} + 72}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722560} {:answer/id #uuid "fada9336-b0f8-542d-9c73-2b2cfd32d2ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{3}\\left(- t + 2\\right)\\sqrt{72 \\left(t - 2\\right)^{2} + 72}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722568}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce610074-5a90-54f0-8399-cb91e4a8db70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{3}\\left|t - 2\\right|\\sqrt{72 \\left(t - 2\\right)^{2} + 72}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722560} :answer-field/id #uuid "87282537-05cf-52b4-a0f2-621d50440c8d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722554}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "08253bfe-4a79-5797-9c99-9e7b20a8c0d2" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the length of the curve defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx&=2 \\left(t - 2\\right)^{3} + 3 \\left(t - 2\\right)^{2} - 3\\\\\ny&=2 \\left(t - 2\\right)^{3} - 3 \\left(t - 2\\right)^{2} + 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfrom $t=0$ to $t=3$?\n\nChoose an integral expression valid on the entire interval. Do not evaluate it.\n\n![](images/78/78c5caf85c0c82de54ea5af8a6cfef3071538dec0af23d3dc7d46c841bccf51f.png)" :question/worked-solution "For parametric arc length, use\n\n$$\nL=\\int_a^b\\sqrt{[x\\prime(t)]^2+[y\\prime(t)]^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nDifferentiate each coordinate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx'(t)&=6 t + 6 \\left(t - 2\\right)^{2} - 12\\\\\ny'(t)&=- 6 t + 6 \\left(t - 2\\right)^{2} + 12.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe cross terms cancel when the two derivative squares are added.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx'(t)^2+y'(t)^2&=72 \\left(t - 2\\right)^{4} + 72 \\left(t - 2\\right)^{2}\\\\\n&=(t - 2)^2\\bigl(72 \\left(t - 2\\right)^{2} + 72\\bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse $\\sqrt{(t - 2)^2}=|t - 2|$. The factor $t - 2$ changes sign inside this interval, so its absolute value must remain.\n\nUse the given parameter bounds:\n\n$$\nL=\\int_{0}^{3}\\left|t - 2\\right|\\sqrt{72 \\left(t - 2\\right)^{2} + 72}\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722545 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03d960df-706d-575b-b9a7-e4437dae92fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045