c-47725fe747bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-1}^{2}\\left(- t - 1\\right)\\sqrt{32 \\left(t + 1\\right)^{2} + 162}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722585} {:answer/id #uuid "ec59f002-19f6-5780-abaa-59ac0467627c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-1}^{2}\\left(t + 1\\right)\\sqrt{32 \\left(t + 1\\right)^{2} + 162}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722595}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "708fb451-3e0f-56ca-ac39-ef6b0a0eca6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-1}^{2}\\left(t + 1\\right)\\sqrt{18 \\left(t + 1\\right)^{2} + 72}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722577} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8599ad4-184b-5057-bf19-3da79cebac85" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722587}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "b56f7b0e-730b-583e-9993-cd6bda7d5311" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the length of the curve defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx&=\\left(t + 1\\right)^{3} + 3 \\left(t + 1\\right)^{2} + 3\\\\\ny&=\\left(t + 1\\right)^{3} - 3 \\left(t + 1\\right)^{2} + 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfrom $t=-1$ to $t=2$?\n\nChoose an integral expression valid on the entire interval. Do not evaluate it.\n\n![](images/bc/bcc1a1b8c0980d38e90a8988565875d87621d7b397f9a8b16bf25523df0dd991.png)" :question/worked-solution "For parametric arc length, use\n\n$$\nL=\\int_a^b\\sqrt{[x\\prime(t)]^2+[y\\prime(t)]^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nDifferentiate each coordinate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx'(t)&=6 t + 3 \\left(t + 1\\right)^{2} + 6\\\\\ny'(t)&=- 6 t + 3 \\left(t + 1\\right)^{2} - 6.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe cross terms cancel when the two derivative squares are added.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx'(t)^2+y'(t)^2&=18 \\left(t + 1\\right)^{4} + 72 \\left(t + 1\\right)^{2}\\\\\n&=(t + 1)^2\\bigl(18 \\left(t + 1\\right)^{2} + 72\\bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse $\\sqrt{(t + 1)^2}=|t + 1|$. The factor $t + 1$ is nonnegative on this interval. Hence $|t + 1|=t + 1$ here.\n\nUse the given parameter bounds:\n\n$$\nL=\\int_{-1}^{2}\\left(t + 1\\right)\\sqrt{18 \\left(t + 1\\right)^{2} + 72}\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722599 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6643fcc0-1751-5968-8733-c971f46c0783" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\sqrt{4 \\sin^{2}{\\left(2 t \\right)} + 4 \\sin^{2}{\\left(4 t \\right)}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722610} {:answer/id #uuid "745f1666-9170-560b-8576-1e22bf06dda4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\sqrt{4 \\sin^{2}{\\left(2 t \\right)} + 64 \\sin^{2}{\\left(4 t \\right)}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722612} {:answer/id #uuid "78cdab7a-a68b-5160-8038-bfe2abb2d8d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\sqrt{8 \\sin^{2}{\\left(2 t \\right)} + 16 \\sin^{2}{\\left(4 t \\right)}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722614} {:answer/id #uuid "9eb31a98-ad2c-5f0d-ac04-8038f126521a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\sqrt{\\sin^{2}{\\left(2 t \\right)} + 256 \\sin^{2}{\\left(4 t \\right)}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722623} {:answer/id #uuid "b8795ca6-5d5f-5693-80a7-edd6fca4612b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\sqrt{8 \\sin^{2}{\\left(2 t \\right)} + 4 \\sin^{2}{\\left(4 t \\right)}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722627}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "745f1666-9170-560b-8576-1e22bf06dda4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\sqrt{4 \\sin^{2}{\\left(2 t \\right)} + 64 \\sin^{2}{\\left(4 t \\right)}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722612} :answer-field/id #uuid "b551a93d-24ea-5141-b1cb-ef275df40cbe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722626}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1ba9f280-6136-576e-af9a-d6cf99540d0d" :question/problem "Which integral gives the arc length of the curve defined by\n\n$$\nx=2 \\cos{\\left(4 t \\right)} - 1,\\qquad y=\\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)} - 2\n$$\n\nfrom $t=0$ to $t=\\frac{\\pi}{2}$? Choose an integral expression. Do not evaluate it." :question/worked-solution "For a parametric curve, use\n\n$$\nL=\\int_a^b\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\right)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t\n$$\n\nDifferentiate with respect to $t$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}&=- 8 \\sin{\\left(4 t \\right)}\\\\\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}&=- 2 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquare the complete derivatives before adding, and retain the parameter limits. The two trig arguments differ, so the Pythagorean identity cannot combine these terms. Substitute and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L&=\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\sqrt{\\left(- 2 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right)^{2} + \\left(- 8 \\sin{\\left(4 t \\right)}\\right)^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\&=\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\sqrt{4 \\sin^{2}{\\left(2 t \\right)} + 64 \\sin^{2}{\\left(4 t \\right)}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722606 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "366aa520-a724-5d3e-be4a-814937c1a16f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{9 \\sin^{2}{\\left(3 t \\right)} + 4 \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} - 4 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722602} {:answer/id #uuid "74a35716-36f2-59d4-a141-32a56192572b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{9 \\sin^{2}{\\left(3 t \\right)} + 4 \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722613} {:answer/id #uuid "7c23e66b-468e-589e-bc06-899420f7ffdf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{36 \\sin^{2}{\\left(3 t \\right)} + 4 \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 4 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722616} {:answer/id #uuid "914e45e9-acb0-56fb-b469-9cfa251c20f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{9 \\sin^{2}{\\left(3 t \\right)} + 16 \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722621} {:answer/id #uuid "a29c991c-e1f3-58d1-9bc8-57c420f856c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{9 \\sin^{2}{\\left(3 t \\right)} + 4 \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 4 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722624}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a29c991c-e1f3-58d1-9bc8-57c420f856c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{9 \\sin^{2}{\\left(3 t \\right)} + 4 \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 4 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722624} :answer-field/id #uuid "54c2968a-05e7-543b-bfe9-46aa90c326d5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722605}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "5ad20f31-1809-5169-b306-cab94e194542" :question/problem "Which integral gives the arc length of the curve defined by\n\n$$\nx=\\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)} - 1,\\qquad y=t + 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 1\n$$\n\nfrom $t=0$ to $t=2$? Choose an integral expression. Do not evaluate it." :question/worked-solution "For a parametric curve, use\n\n$$\nL=\\int_a^b\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\right)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t\n$$\n\nDifferentiate with respect to $t$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}&=- 3 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\\\\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}&=2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquare the complete derivatives before adding, and retain the parameter limits. Expand the binomial square, including its signed cross term. Substitute and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L&=\\int_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{\\left(2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 1\\right)^{2} + \\left(- 3 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\right)^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\&=\\int_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{9 \\sin^{2}{\\left(3 t \\right)} + 4 \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 4 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722608 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1752fcb1-bd9a-58f1-b7e6-64bcaedddf07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{17 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 14 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 98}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722598} {:answer/id #uuid "2d2f5a77-e715-59b1-8946-17da45d8fd53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{17 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 14 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 49}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722601} {:answer/id #uuid "6e0cadc6-cbc9-5a19-b5fa-46ac314d8ee6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{17 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 49}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722611} {:answer/id #uuid "dfafa557-2883-5fc1-8c79-e1689682a847" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{16 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 7 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 49}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722628} {:answer/id #uuid "f9d109c0-62fc-56f1-bd27-6236a1770031" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{17 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 7 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 49}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722630}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d2f5a77-e715-59b1-8946-17da45d8fd53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{17 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 14 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 49}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722601} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7e6f45a-accf-5a48-914e-bdf48cfb2d11" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722629}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "60d8d29d-73a6-5356-a3ed-a47171a121d5" :question/problem "Which integral gives the arc length of the curve defined by\n\n$$\nx=7 t - \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 2,\\qquad y=4 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 2\n$$\n\nfrom $t=-1$ to $t=1$? Choose an integral expression. Do not evaluate it." :question/worked-solution "For a parametric curve, use\n\n$$\nL=\\int_a^b\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\right)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t\n$$\n\nDifferentiate with respect to $t$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}&=\\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 7\\\\\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}&=- 4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquare the complete derivatives before adding, and retain the parameter limits. Expand the binomial square, then collect the squared sine terms. Substitute and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L&=\\int_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{\\left(\\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 7\\right)^{2} + \\left(- 4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\&=\\int_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{17 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 14 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 49}\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722617 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "049b7e44-da86-5a7c-aa48-1f7374912376" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{10 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 36}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722597} {:answer/id #uuid "854ec20f-1950-569b-8ef5-c57c4c24f665" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{10 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} - 6 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 36}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722618} {:answer/id #uuid "8975d37a-71e9-5e5a-bf53-369a3f607c29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{\\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} - 12 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 36}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722619} {:answer/id #uuid "b4a42a70-0c75-554e-9103-d46bd5310803" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{9 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} - 6 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 36}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722625} {:answer/id #uuid "fafd6913-1f23-5ab4-8e5b-d0198c633c8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{10 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} - 12 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 36}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722631}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fafd6913-1f23-5ab4-8e5b-d0198c633c8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{10 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} - 12 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 36}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722631} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a2c98c5-2af0-585d-9610-9a16f4f45258" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722615}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7c948b16-b6a7-5204-b759-64ed93598771" :question/problem "Which integral gives the arc length of the curve defined by\n\n$$\nx=3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 1,\\qquad y=6 t + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 2\n$$\n\nfrom $t=0$ to $t=2$? Choose an integral expression. Do not evaluate it." :question/worked-solution "For a parametric curve, use\n\n$$\nL=\\int_a^b\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\right)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t\n$$\n\nDifferentiate with respect to $t$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}&=- 3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\\\\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}&=6 - \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquare the complete derivatives before adding, and retain the parameter limits. Expand the binomial square, then collect the squared sine terms. Substitute and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L&=\\int_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{\\left(6 - \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)^{2} + \\left(- 3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\&=\\int_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{10 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} - 12 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 36}\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722620 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "450cd6d3-6091-5a0d-8ef8-0c7094aba717" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{1}4 e^{- \\frac{t}{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #